# Shell scripts must always be checked out with LF endings, even on Windows
# (where core.autocrlf=true is common). A CRLF shebang makes the script fail
# to run inside WSL with:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# This matters because README tells users to run `bash setup-dev-tools.sh`
# directly, which bypasses the CR-stripping that wsl-setup.bat does.
*.sh text eol=lf
